    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d85">

                <pb facs="0229" n="63" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg63"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/2608</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Wheeler to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 13, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Complete text of the note to China was for the first time published here today,
                    copied from Shanghai newspapers. Comment shows decided betterment in feeling and
                    I am confidentially informed that Foreign Office is making strong efforts to
                    this end. The Vice Minister for Foreign Office told me this morning that the
                    published reports to the effect that Japan was framing a “protest” were without
                    foundation and that whatever communication was made on the subject would be of
                    the most friendly tone.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wheeler</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
